UID:stimuleringsfonds-suriname-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T141447Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Suriname 2027 (Par
 amaribo\, Moengo\, Frederiksdorp)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or interdisciplinary maker f
 or a three-month residency in 2027 across three locations in Suriname: Par
 amaribo\, Moengo and Frederiksdorp\, each with its own cultural\, historic
 al and social context. The residency is inspired by the Surinamese notion 
 of alakondre (literally 'all countries')\, which symbolises living togethe
 r in cultural diversity and emphasises the power of coexisting differences
 . Rather than simply promoting harmony\, alakondre acknowledges historical
  inequalities\, cultural sensitivities and tensions ensuing from colonial 
 and socio-economic realities\, which demands openness and critical awarene
 ss of your position as a creative practitioner\; personal stories\, whethe
 r family history or questions of identity\, can provide powerful entry poi
 nts. A network of local partners supports the residency\, and at each loca
 tion a local maker selected by Surinamese partner organisations works alon
 gside you\, creating natural opportunities for creative exchange and dialo
 gue. ELIGIBILITY: you are an individual designer\, architect or spatial pr
 actitioner\; you are established in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (the Ne
 therlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maar
 ten)\; you are registered in the register of the Dutch Chamber of Commerce
  (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands\
 ; and you have run a professional practice within the creative industries 
 for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or collaborative p
 artnerships\, nor to current recipients of the Talent Development Grant Sc
 heme\, the Open Call Self-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design
  Practices ABCSSS\; accepting this open call means you cannot apply to tho
 se schemes and open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for the thr
 ee-month residency\; one position is awarded. Assessment takes the form of
  a tender: an external advisory committee ranks proposals on the artistic 
 quality of the work\, the quality of the development plan and the motivati
 on in relation to the residency's objective\, and the highest-scoring prop
 osal is awarded. Decision within eight weeks of the closing date. Submit v
 ia the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund
  NL) with local partner organisations in Suriname\nLocation: Residency tak
 es place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\, Moengo and Frederiks
 dorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\
 , Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherla
 nds) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom of the Nethe
 rlands.\nAward: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for a three-month residency\, paid by t
 he Creative Industries Fund NL. One residency position is awarded. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: Three months in 2027\, moving between Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-residency-suriname?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-suriname
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlan
 ds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Ki
 ngdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the
  Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cove-park-awarded-residencies-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T141447Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261212
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cove Park Awarded Residencies 2027-2028 (Scotland\, UK\, 
 Central and South America and diasporas)
DESCRIPTION:Cove Park's biennial call for fully funded Awarded Residencies 
 at its 50-acre rural residency site in Argyll\, on the west coast of Scotl
 and\, programmed between May 2027 and December 2028. Residencies run from 
 2 weeks up to 12 weeks (average four weeks) and can be split across the tw
 o years around caring or work commitments\; international residents can co
 unt slow-travel time as part of the funded period. Open to artists\, creat
 ive practitioners\, writers\, translators and researchers in all art forms
  and at every career stage\, including collectives and collaborative group
 s\; no formal qualification needed. Priorities include work responding to 
 climate breakdown\, sound artists and musicians (new Sound Studio)\, and w
 ork on home\, place\, language (Scots\, Gaelic\, BSL)\, displacement and b
 elonging. No final presentation is required. ELIGIBILITY: based in the UK\
 , Central America or South America\; Central and South American diaspora a
 rtists based in Europe or North America\; or born in Scotland and living e
 lsewhere. Anyone in full- or part-time formal education on 11 December 202
 6 is not eligible. SUPPORT: GBP 775 per week fee\; travel allowance (Scotl
 and GBP 65 to 100 Central Belt\, up to GBP 200 Borders/Highlands/Islands\;
  rest of UK up to GBP 250\; Europe up to GBP 400\; other international up 
 to GBP 1\,250)\; materials up to GBP 150\; visa support\; private self-cat
 ering accommodation (suitable for collaborators and those attending with c
 hildren) and private studios. An Application Access Bursary (e.g. to pay a
  support worker) is available for applicants facing barriers due to disabi
 lity or neurodivergence\; request it from Alex Marrs by 30 November 2026. 
 Video or audio applications accepted. Applicants are asked not to use gene
 rative AI in their application. APPLY via the online form: 500-word statem
 ent\, 100-word bio\, CV\, up to 8 images or video/audio links or writing s
 amples. SELECTION: shortlisting by the programme team and former residents
 \; shortlist notified by 12 February 2027\; Zoom interviews the week of 22
  February 2027. Contact: Alex Marrs\, alex@covepark.org. DEADLINE: Friday 
 11 December 2026\, 5pm GMT.\n\nOrganisation: Cove Park\nLocation: Cove Par
 k\, Peaton Hill\, Argyll and Bute\, Scotland (in person\, private self-cat
 ering accommodation and studio). Open to people based in the UK\, Central 
 or South America\, Central and South American diaspora artists based in Eu
 rope or North America\, and Scotland-born artists living anywhere. Student
 s in formal education are not eligible.\nAward: Fully funded: GBP 775 per 
 week fee (VAT inclusive\, freelance)\, travel allowance (Scotland GBP 65 t
 o 200\, rest of UK up to GBP 250\, Europe up to GBP 400\, other internatio
 nal up to GBP 1\,250)\, materials up to GBP 150 for studio-based practitio
 ners\, private accommodation and studio\, visa and access support. Applica
 tion Access Bursary available (request by 30 November 2026). No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: 2 to 12 weeks (average 4)\, between May 2027 and Decembe
 r 2028\n\nMore: https://covepark.org/awarded-residencies-2027-2028/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://covepark.org/awarded-residencies-2027-2028/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cove Park\, Peaton Hill\, Argyll and Bute\, Scotland (in person\, 
 private self-catering accommodation and studio). Open to people based in t
 he UK\, Central or South America\, Central and South American diaspora art
 ists based in Europe or North America\, and Scotland-born artists living a
 nywhere. Students in formal education are not eligible.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
